{:answer/id #uuid "03385eae-78c4-52c5-b742-e2827129a23f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{4})_{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153782} {:answer/id #uuid "0f723d6f-e8f8-5491-9b7a-0a54aba69a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{25}{36})_{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153783}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3c500d12-f63a-586b-ba7d-e1463f6d5905" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153778}] :question/id #uuid "26c83d50-4529-5044-8c8f-50bafb4f14f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-135602" :question/problem "What is $(0.25)_{6}$ written as a fraction in base $10$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157595 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b6e01e1-4a3f-595a-9b3f-45a980de3650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153815} {:answer/id #uuid "eed340e5-56a4-5ccc-bab1-0efae14406aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153816} {:answer/id #uuid "fa783059-bf91-58a5-88df-51e405e2e194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153817} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc18689-8da1-57e9-87ce-eceb56d03d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153818} {:answer/id #uuid "7465be06-c100-5781-88c3-8c72bbce7127" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153819}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fa8062cd-bc6e-5063-a3e1-77b2287ef64c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153814}] :question/id #uuid "413a4dcf-58fb-5b90-a1d5-81eb32b89d3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-138288" :question/problem "Given that $X∼Po(\\frac{49}{16})$, what is $SD[X]$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157606 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a69b927d-fd51-516f-aae0-cf0da09a7720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153881} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ba8dfc-c937-598b-a9a5-dc59f7c01e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153882} {:answer/id #uuid "eb402453-8e9e-5d3c-a06e-96fbfc84d9da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153883} {:answer/id #uuid "f418ec1e-ed9d-5bce-a47f-762f1c808098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153884} {:answer/id #uuid "63a0df93-12b0-5a94-8153-cab57c777d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb402453-8e9e-5d3c-a06e-96fbfc84d9da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153883} :answer-field/id #uuid "07e9af8f-c53a-563f-b1d5-c1fb676708fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186153880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d40b16f4-c022-5679-aaee-aa1be46926d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-149708" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3{x}^{2}+4}{5},\\,0<x<1\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{20},$ compute $\\text{E}[2X-{X}^{3}+1].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X-{X}^{3}+1] & =2\\text{E}[X]-\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]+\\text{E}[1] \\\\  & =2\\text{E}[X]-\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the third raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\cdot (\\frac{3{x}^{2}+4}{5})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{5}+\\frac{4}{5}{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{6}+\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{4})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}+\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{20}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]=\\frac{3}{10}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X-{X}^{3}+1] & =2\\text{E}[X]-\\text{E}[{X}^{3}]+1 \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{11}{20}-\\frac{3}{10}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{10}-\\frac{3}{10}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "325c4fe7-ef6a-5e8d-8834-207b93321aa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "325c4fe7-ef6a-5e8d-8834-207b93321aa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290836} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b71d412-055e-5d46-8827-61f0331a39bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "284e775b-ea6f-5b7b-9ed5-737476983233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "284e775b-ea6f-5b7b-9ed5-737476983233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290797} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ccb952e-8a19-50a0-aa5c-9c9e509b5dd7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3717499f-854b-5192-9745-639bb9e5ec4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3717499f-854b-5192-9745-639bb9e5ec4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290857} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4adfdcb-0c88-5e37-a712-4903eabcf1ae" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292381} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c00233b-4a30-51b5-9f6c-ea30ad82d7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c00233b-4a30-51b5-9f6c-ea30ad82d7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291229} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc63de8-0f44-5858-a25f-84025013b44a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4142f862-e575-5cdf-acae-f1cf787219fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-252925" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | $6$ | {{field-1}} | $-3$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\operatorname{sin}⁡({J}_{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}))=\\frac{1}{12}\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | $6$ | {{field-3}} | $-3$ |  |\n|  | $0$ | $0$ | $6$ | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $6$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ $n=4,$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nSince $n=4,$ we need to compute the first $4-1=3$ derivatives of $f:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & {f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & \\frac{1}{2!}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & \\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\ 0 & f(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & {f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & \\frac{1}{2!}{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & {f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & f(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & -\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & -\\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{12} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6\\sqrt{3} & -3 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 6 & 6\\sqrt{3} & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 6\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]
